{"model": "gemini-3.8-flash", "qid": "q006", "dataset": "gsm8k", "para": 1, "sample": "g", "temp": 0.0, "answer": "6", "correct": false, "content_len": 765, "reasoning_len": 0, "snippet": "We are given:\n\n- Total days: 30\n- 12 good days, 8 bad days,  ... s (3 groups of 8):\n- First 8: good\n- Second 8: bad\n- Third 8: neutral\n\nSo far:\n- Good: 8\n- Bad: 8\n- Neutral: 8\n\nBut over 30 days there were 12 good, 8 bad, 10 neutral total.\n\nThat means the last 6 days (days 25–30) contributed:\n- Good: 12 - 8 = 4\n- Bad: 8 - 8 = 0\n- Neutral: 10 - 8 = 2\n\nSo in days 25–30, there were 4 good, 2 neutral.\n\nNow the next 3 days were: good, neutral, good.\nThat's 2 more good days.\n\nQuestion: \"how many good days were left in the month?\"\n\nThis likely means: how many good days occurred in the remaining 9 days (days 25–30 plus the next 3)?\n\nFrom above: 4 good (in days 25–30) + 2 good (next 3 days) = 6.\n\nAnswer: 6", "usage": {"pt": 403, "ct": 311}, "t": 1792302210.4}
